Applicant tracking

ats-core, candidate-card, candidate-row, candidate-detail, assessment-form,
pipeline-board, and ats are a clean-room hiring board for a CRM. The
arrangement was observed in an unlicensed recruiting mock (a public social
post of a candidate kanban, a list, and an evaluation drawer). No source,
markup, copy, colors, icons, photos, or assets were copied. Stages are
derived by the host with getStage. A move is onMoveCandidate and may
reject. Tones and extra actions are props. Spanish is the default chrome.
atsLabelsEn is the English set. The default zone is America/Mexico_City
and formats use es-MX. Dates reuse the existing date-range helpers. The
catalog demo is Taller Nube, a fictional studio. The people, jobs, and
scorecards are invented. A second example at /examples/ats/eduardoretana
dresses the same pieces with stage labels and badge classes observed on
the public eduardoretana.com app. The people, phones, and scorecards on
that page are invented. The board reuses search-field, segmented-control,
and the host sheet. Answer no if the CLI asks to overwrite a primitive
the host already has, or date-range when the host already has it. The
items ship no theme.

