OrganUI (healthcare and life sciences)

Retana UI includes components adapted from OrganUI (MIT):

  https://organui.com  ·  https://organui.com/docs/licences

Copyright (c) 2026 OrganUI

OrganUI has no paid or Pro tier; every registry item is MIT. The pieces were
ported from OrganUI's Base UI style onto this registry's Radix primitives.
By explicit ui-system exception (docs/ui-system-exceptions.md, EX-01), the
anatomy, imaging and molecular scenes keep OrganUI's original realistic
colours and 3D lighting (organ-*, organ-viewer, molecule-viewer, dna-helix,
dermatome-map, image-viewer). UI chrome stays on host theme tokens.
Interface text stays in English and can be overridden by props.

3D models are NOT copied into this repository. Each organ item loads a GLB at
runtime from a commit-pinned URL in the matching github.com/organui/*-3d
repository, and the model keeps its own licence (CC0 1.0, CC BY 4.0,
CC BY-SA 2.1 JP or CC BY-SA 4.0, per model). The BY licences require credit:
the viewer shows it by default. If you pass `attribution={false}`, credit the
model elsewhere in your interface. ShareAlike applies to adapted models.

Sample data: the growth-chart demo uses an illustrative curve, not WHO data
(WHO standards are GPL-3 and need permission for commercial use). The
molecule demo fetches PDB 1CRN (wwPDB, CC0). The head phantom, synthetic ECG,
vitals, lab and medication examples are generated and MIT.

Adapted items:

- anatomy-tree, vital-signs, ecg-trace, body-map, dermatome-map, lab-results,
  growth-chart, medication-schedule, image-viewer, organ-viewer,
  molecule-viewer, dna-helix
- organ-* (43 organ and tissue models)
- organ-explorer, anatomy-workspace, organ-switcher (blocks)
